        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.294,
            0.67,
            0.748,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many negative numbers are there?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.696,
            0.862,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Bela’s Building of Fun had only six floors above and five floors below. That is numbers – 5 to + 6. In the mine above, we have numbers from – 200 to + 180. But we can imagine larger buildings or mineshafts. Just as positive numbers + 1, + 2, + 3, ... keep going up without an end, similarly, negative numbers – 1, – 2, – 3, ... keep going down. Positive and negative numbers, with zero, are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "integers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". They go both ways from 0: … – 4, – 3, – 2, – 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, …"
            }
          ]
        },
